.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt NINJA 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ninja
.Nd build a generated dependency graph
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar target ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads
.Pa build.ninja
and runs the commands needed to update the requested targets, or its
default targets when none are named.
A higher-level tool usually generates this file.
.Fl C Ar directory
changes directory first;
.Fl f Ar file
reads another build file;
.Fl j Ar jobs
limits concurrent jobs;
.Fl n
prints commands without running them;
.Fl v
prints each full command.
.Ql ninja --help
describes the other options, and
.Ql ninja -t list
lists its tools for inspecting a build.
.Pp
The x86-64 GNU root installs the project's Linux build, version 1.13.2,
under
.Pa /opt/ninja
when built with
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=ninja
or
.Ql GNU_AGENTS=all .
.Pa /usr/bin/ninja
and
.Pa /bin/ninja
link to it.
The Apache License 2.0 is in
.Pa /opt/ninja/COPYING .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa build.ninja
build rules and dependencies
.It Pa .ninja_log
completed commands and their recorded times
.It Pa .ninja_deps
recorded header dependencies
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ninja -C build -j 4
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr make 1
.Pp
.Lk https://ninja-build.org/manual.html "The Ninja manual"
